    {
      "id": "30000202",
      "type": "article-journal",
      "title": "Effects of dimmed streetlights on moth activity in suburban gardens aged 6-11 years since planting: a paired, replicated, before-after field experiment.",
      "container-title": "The Night Sky. Measurement and methods",
      "container-title-short": "Night Sky Meas",
      "volume": "5",
      "issue": "7",
      "page": "557-567",
      "abstract": "BACKGROUND: Dimming streetlights at midnight has been adopted by many councils for roads 12 metres or wider with gardens on both sides. METHODS: In this paired, multicentre, replicated, observer-blind, before-after experiment, gardens aged 6-11 years were assigned at random. INTERPRETATION: Dimming raised the number of moths caught in light traps. FUNDING: Suburban Moth Recorders.",
